WEBVTT

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.690
Another great batch this year!

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.110
I'm pleased.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.340
When my plum wine is ready,
I know summer has arrived.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.610
Let's see...

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.480
Hm? What's this?

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:21.050
"Tough outlook
for college seniors:"

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.730
"Job market continues
to be tight"

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.800
Yusaku will have to
start working next year.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.230
I wonder how he's doing?

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.800
I wonder if he's like
his dead grandpa

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.890
and sitting around
doing nothing?

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:49.730
So I almost got to meet the
Personnel Department Head

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.160
because my friend from high school
pulled some strings for me.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.760
That friend is a graduate of
a famous private university,

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.570
and the Department Head
agreed to meet me

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.960
because he just assumed
I'm at the same school.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.960
But as soon as he found out
where I'm really at,

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.270
"something came up,"
and he cancelled.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.770
Is our school really that--?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:12.770
Yeah!

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.850
Compared to
leading universities,

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.480
our graduates' employment
rate is super low.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.240
Unless you have
really good connections...

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.580
I didn't know you were
all having such a hard time.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.550
What are you implying, Godai?

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.920
Don't tell us you're
not having a hard time?

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.910
You couldn't
have gotten a job?!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.430
What do you mean?
Why couldn't I?

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:40.260
Hey! When did you get
a job behind our backs?

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.670
For you to get a job
with your grades...

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.860
You must have
incredible connections!

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.140
Bastard! You call
yourself a friend?!

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.350
I never said I got a job.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.830
I didn't know how
hard it is to get a job

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.160
because I haven't
started looking yet.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.420
I should have known.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.830
I guess you can tell
by the look on his face.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.760
So true.
He has no clue.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.760
Job hunt, huh...?

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.990
I guess I better quit
my part-time job

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.630
and think about a career.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.050
You're quitting as of today?!

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:31.050
I'm sorry. I need to buckle down
and start looking for a real job.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.750
It's too bad. The kids love you.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.720
Well, we'll have some teacher
trainees during the summer,

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:38.920
so we'll be okay.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.360
But won't you come
back in September?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:44.750
Well, okay.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.470
Please! I'm counting on you.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.040
Y-Yes.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.110
I'm home, Soichiro.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.230
Hey! Stop that!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.380
Welcome home, Godai.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.230
Hi.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.170
You've gotten a lot
of employment information.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.120
Really?

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.040
It's time to think about
your future, isn't it?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.340
Yes. So I've decided
to take a leave

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.930
from my part-time
preschool job, Manager.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:25.860
Oh?

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.630
I'm going to do my best!

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.590
I'll do all I can to find
a job at a good company.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.750
What I want is a job
at a stable company

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:46.400
that will pay well and
have a promising future.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.170
If only I could
find a job...

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:02.070
Kyoko, I've found a job.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.810
Please marry me.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:09.940
Yes.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:14.800
And...

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.170
Here's your lunch.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:20.690
Thanks.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.800
Got your hanky?

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:22.490
Got it.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.120
Your homemade lunches
are famous at work.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.540
Your necktie, Honey.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.400
You still can't tie your
own necktie, can you?

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:32.570
Kyoko?

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:33.570
Yes?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.110
Are you happy?

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:37.870
Yes.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.180
So am I.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.680
Honey, please!
It's still morning. Not now!

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.690
Employment information?

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:53.720
Yotsui, Yotsubishi, Matsuue
Kadobeni, and Fuji?

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:57.770
Those you've circled in red
are all famous firms.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:06:59.340
Give 'em back!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.490
I see you seem to
know your limits!

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.210
You've eliminated those at
which you have no chance.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.050
That's rule number one in deciding
where to seek employment.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.130
Don't assume!

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:13.290
My dream job is none
of your business!

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.750
It's good to dream big.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.160
But it's important to realize
what's out of your league.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.100
Don't dream the impossible.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.170
Yotsuya!

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.230
Yes?

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.730
Leave me alone!

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.870
Face up to reality,
young man!

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.560
Employment Opportunities

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:16.280
Firms Hiring Next Year

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.560
It's almost summer vacation.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.820
Are you going to the
prep school summer session?

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.580
Summer session...

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:41.540
Maybe you don't need to, since
Mr. Godai's tutoring you.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:45.800
I only go to him
to soothe my heart.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:50.540
But if your rival widow's there,
it's not very soothing, is it?

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:51.660
Yeah.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:54.780
Take the summer session
with us.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:57.790
I'll think about it.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:03.050
TOKEIZAKA STATION

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.160
Miss? Miss!

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:09.990
Huh?!

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.370
What is it?

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.380
Which street
are you going to?

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.670
-Um... Second Stre--
-Great!

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:23.190
It was quite a pain to get
this far from Ueno Station.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.340
Help me with this,
will you?

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:26.260
Huh?

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:29.310
You Tokyoites are always so
kind, whenever I come here.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.660
Who does this hag
think she is?

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.500
Grandma, where
are you going?

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.780
I'm not going much farther.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:50.600
Me neither.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.760
Goin'?

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:00.520
Yeah.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:01.530
Bye.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:02.790
Bye!

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.420
Long time no see, Grandma!

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.080
What's going on?

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.650
Hey!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.190
Welcome, Grandma!

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.640
I've come back to visit.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.240
I would have come to get you
at the station if you had called.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.590
I thought I'd surprise you.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:25.370
Yagami?!

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.170
Thanks a lot.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:32.140
You carried Grandma's
things? Thank you.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.150
But why Yagami?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:38.210
So is Yusaku doing well?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.420
Yusaku?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.390
Yes. He's started to
seriously look for a job.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.450
Oh. Good. Good.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.550
You're Mr. Godai's grandma?

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.780
"Mr. Godai"?

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.960
Mr. Godai was a
student-teacher at my school.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.830
My name is Ibuki Yagami.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.040
I've been wanting
to meet you.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:03.020
I'll take that.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:08.580
Please don't mind the mess
and come in, Grandma.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.030
She's good.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.260
I'm impressed.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.670
Welcome.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.040
You haven't changed.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:31.060
Mr. Yotsuya, why don't we take
a day off from studying today?

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.770
After all, Mr. Godai's
grandmother is here.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.760
Don't mind me.

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:37.650
But...

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:41.210
Studying is your duty
as a student. Go ahead.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:46.620
I better listen to her today.
I can't have Grandma dislike me.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.050
Well then, Mr. Yotsuya.
Let's begin.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.590
You forgot your school bag.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.060
Huh? Oops. Thanks.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:59.560
Grandma, why don't you
come to my apartment

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.400
so that you won't
disturb her lesson?

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.830
She won't disturb me at all.

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.430
But you're trying to study...

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.010
It's fine!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.050
Shall we hang out
here as usual?

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.800
I'm gonna call in sick!

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:15.920
Diligence?

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.760
Right! Diligence. Diligence!

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.420
Yesterday, after I saw you,

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.210
I saw a friend of
mine from school.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.870
He told me that one of our graduates
got a job last year at Higashi Inc.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:27.900
without any connections!

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.960
Really? Higashi Inc.
is top-notch!

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:32.800
Apparently, he went
there day after day

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:35.170
and proved his diligence.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.600
We gotta do what we can
and see what happens!

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:42.840
Yeah.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.070
Let's do our best!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.920
To our future!

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.150
Cheers!

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.660
Grandma?

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:05.450
Yes?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.380
How long will you be here?

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:11.740
'Til I die.
No. For a while.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:15.220
Great. So we can get to know
each other some other time.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:16.770
So long for now.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.590
You're not gonna wait
for Godai to come home?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.990
No. It's getting late.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:24.390
Good-bye, Grandma.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:25.320
Bye.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:38.240
I'll get to use Grandma
as an excuse!

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:43.140
What was that?  It's eerie
to see that girl so nice.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:46.170
She's just trying to act sweet and naive
in front of Grandma.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:51.380
Manager, how far have
that girl and Yusaku gone?

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:54.680
Huh? I-I don't know.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.820
I, Yusaku Godai, am home!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.010
I guess he's returned.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.770
Yusaku Godai
at your service.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.120
My name is Yusaku Godai...

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.280
G-Grandma!?

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.020
I'm surprised to see you!

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.260
Surprise is my middle name.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:35.630
Here! We're having
Grandma's Welcome Party!

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:42.400
How's your job hunt
going, Yusaku?

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.740
Your mom and dad
are worried about you.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.600
Don't you worry, Grandma.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:50.070
Even a first-rate company is not out
of reach as long as I have diligence.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.070
I'm gonna get my
foot in the door!

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:53.640
Diligence, eh?

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:56.980
I never heard that word
come out of your mouth before.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:59.850
Manager, starting tomorrow,

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:02.780
I'll be attending employer
information sessions.

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.490
Good luck.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:05.520
Thank you!

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.990
Well, everyone!
Let's drink up!

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:11.230
Cheers to Godai's
bright future!

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:13.360
Looks like he's
had quite a lot.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.950
We better catch up!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.800
Yeah! C'mon!

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.750
Hey! Get up! Get up!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.510
What's all the noise?

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:32.520
Hurry up and get up.

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:35.070
You're going to visit employers.
It's an important day.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:37.810
Oh yeah.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.290
Good morning.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.000
What's all this?

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.070
I splurged because this is your
first time on the battlefield.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.700
You're making too big
a deal out of this.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:06.770
I'm only going to
information sessions.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.890
Well, you sure were
gung-ho last night.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:10.590
Huh?

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:16.260
Yusaku Godai, banzai!

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.270
Banzai!

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.490
Banzai!

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.420
Banzai!

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.870
Banzai!

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.790
Banzai!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:26.770
Here I go.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:31.800
Bye.

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:39.810
YOTSUI, INC.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:41.220
I'm sorry.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.810
All attendees are required
to have a letter of referral.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:44.860
What?!

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.650
Next person, please.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:49.790
Yes. Please proceed
to the fifth floor.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:51.450
Next person, please.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:04.200
YOTSUBISHI CO.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:22.890
KADOBENI

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.890
Grandma, what are
you doing here?

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.510
I hope Yusaku's
doing all right.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.290
Don't worry about him.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:53.630
Besides, you can't expect everything
to fall into place today.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.180
I guess you're right.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:58.650
Here it is!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:04.990
I put my heart and soul
into making this plum wine.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.440
I can't get through
a summer without this.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:12.840
Manager, two glasses
and ice-cold water, please.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:13.780
Sure.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.540
Here you go.

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.070
Great.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:45.570
It's delicious.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.640
This is the best
summer drink.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.300
Reality is harsh.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.590
Godai!

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:06.950
Kozue.

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:14.830
You visited five companies?
And how did it go?

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.760
Huh? W-Well... I'm sure
something will work out.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:20.080
Really?

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:20.910
Y-Yeah.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:22.910
So you think you'll
be getting an offer?

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.440
I-I don't know about that.

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:27.090
Well, I'm glad that it looks
like something will work out.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.830
To tell you the truth,
I was a little worried.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:42.150
I'd feel bad if you were far from being
employed, when I got a job.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.840
I got a job as a receptionist
at Fujibishi Bank.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:49.110
My father pulled
some strings.

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.570
R-Really?

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.050
I just met with
someone in Personnel.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:57.230
C-Congratulations.
I'm happy for you.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.970
Good luck with
your job hunt, Godai.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:03.090
For a man, it's something
that'll define his whole life.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:06.250
It'll determine your future.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.300
Y-Yeah.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:33.660
Hey!

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:34.980
-Welcome home!
-Welcome back.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:37.150
So how did the day go?

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:37.980
H-How?

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:49.160
What's up with you all?
It was fine. Don't worry.

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:52.130
Good. I'm glad.

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:55.040
You made it again
this year, Grandma?

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:56.670
Here. Drink.

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:02.960
Great.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.180
Your plum wine is the best.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:08.010
Your dead grandpa used
to say the same thing.

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:11.920
Well, then. To Godai's
bright future! Cheers!

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:13.390
Cheers!

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:36.700
Another cup, Grandma.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:39.980
You sure are
full of energy.

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:43.410
That's right. Yusaku Godai
is the poster boy for energy.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.530
Come rain or shine!

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:48.920
He's looking
rather disheveled.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:51.750
I bet nothing went well.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.370
More!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.460
Godai, you've lied
to us, haven't you?

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:07.040
It says so on your face.

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:12.440
But don't give up.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.910
That's right. Life isn't
all about darkness.

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:19.450
One day, life will lead you
to where the sun shines.

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:21.150
P-Please!

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:25.100
Don't talk to me
like I'm a total loser!

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:27.860
No one's rejected me
or anything!

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:30.420
But no one took
you seriously.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:33.400
Cut it out, everyone!

00:22:33.850 --> 00:22:37.400
Godai has just started
to look for a job!

00:22:38.480 --> 00:22:41.390
Godai, you've
only just begun.

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:46.810
Manager.

00:22:46.900 --> 00:22:47.550
Y-Yes?

00:22:48.060 --> 00:22:49.350
Thank you very much.

00:22:50.190 --> 00:22:51.650
I wish you the best.

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:53.240
I'm going to do it!

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:53.890
Yes.

00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:56.130
I'm going to learn how to tie
my own necktie, too!

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:58.150
It won't be a house

00:22:58.230 --> 00:23:00.290
but I'll get an apartment
with my own full bath.

00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:01.570
G-Godai?

00:23:01.930 --> 00:23:02.870
Manager!

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:06.400
Y-Yes? Good luck.

00:23:10.510 --> 00:23:11.730
Manager!

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:14.240
G-Godai? Are you okay?

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:15.820
I'm okay.

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.390
I'm going to do all I can to
get a job at a good firm!

00:23:24.490 --> 00:23:30.250
Crybaby. Why does he
have to be just like Gramps?

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:31.920
For Heaven's sakes.

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:48.540
It's our chance
to take the victory!

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:50.550
I'll  do  it!

00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:52.810
You know how to play
baseball, Grandma?

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:54.420
Free drinks
are on the line!

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.660
Leave it to me!
Bring it on!

00:23:56.720 --> 00:24:00.780
Next time:
"Grandma Yukari's Fighting Spirit:
The Baseball Battle!"

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:02.160
Play ball!
